Well, the bug is that `slice` excludes its end index, and `arr.length - 1` leaves out the last element. Use `arr.length` as the end:

```js
function lastN(arr, n) {
  return arr.slice(arr.length - n);
}

console.log(lastN([1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 2)); // [4, 5]
```

With one argument, `slice` takes everything from that start index through the end of the array.

